From 553d48abc89d17f5087f4297877604aadf5562c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:54:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: wireless: bcmdhd: handle NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3 in
 wl_set_wpa_version()

wpa_supplicant 2.11 signals WPA3-Personal (SAE) to the driver with
NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3 only; 2.10 used NL80211_WPA_VERSION_2 for the same
connection. wl_set_wpa_version() knows VERSION_1 and VERSION_2 and falls
through to WPA_AUTH_DISABLED for anything else, so with 2.11 the firmware
performs an open association carrying an SAE RSN IE and the AP
deauthenticates it with reason 13 (invalid IE). With SAE selected as the
preferred AKM on a WPA2/WPA3 transition SSID this makes such networks
unjoinable; NetworkManager 1.54 always offers SAE, so on Ubuntu 26.04 the
AP6275P (BCM43752, Orange Pi 5B) could not join a mixed-mode network at
all.

Treat VERSION_3 like VERSION_2: wl_set_key_mgmt() then refines wpa_auth
from the AKM suite (SAE -> WPA3_AUTH_SAE_PSK) exactly as it did with 2.10.
This mirrors brcmf_set_wpa_version() in the upstream brcmfmac driver.

Tested on Orange Pi 5B (AP6275P, fw 18.35.387.23.146) against a UniFi
WPA2/WPA3 SSID with PMF optional on 2.4 GHz: wpa_supplicant 2.10 joins
(SAE, PMF), 2.11 is deauthenticated with reason 13 on every attempt;
nl80211 debug shows the only relevant difference is WPA Versions 0x2 vs
0x4 in the connect request.

Root cause and fix were worked out with the help of an LLM assistant
(Claude); the analysis and the hardware test are the submitter's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/wl_cfg80211.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/wl_cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/wl_cfg80211.c
index 262fe27dbb06..af3f47c67325 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/wl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rockchip_wlan/rkwifi/bcmdhd/wl_cfg80211.c
@@ -4938,6 +4938,16 @@ wl_set_wpa_version(struct net_device *dev, struct cfg80211_connect_params *sme)
 	else if (sme->crypto.wpa_versions & NL80211_WPA_VERSION_2)
 		val = WPA2_AUTH_PSK|
 			WPA2_AUTH_UNSPECIFIED;
+	else if (sme->crypto.wpa_versions & NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3)
+		/* WPA3 (SAE/OWE): wpa_supplicant >= 2.11 signals it with
+		 * NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3 alone, where 2.10 sent VERSION_2.
+		 * Start from the WPA2 set so wl_set_key_mgmt() refines it from
+		 * the AKM (SAE -> WPA3_AUTH_SAE_PSK) exactly as before; the old
+		 * fall-through to WPA_AUTH_DISABLED made the firmware join open
+		 * with an SAE RSN IE and the AP deauthenticated with reason 13.
+		 */
+		val = WPA2_AUTH_PSK|
+			WPA2_AUTH_UNSPECIFIED;
 	else
 		val = WPA_AUTH_DISABLED;
 
-- 
2.53.0

